  "description": "SBF-SEM data for regions of the liver.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Data Overview",
      "anchor": "data-overview",
      "content": [
        {
          "component": "ContentParagraph",
          "content": [
            "This human liver tissue highlights the 3D architecture of the periportal region using serial block-face scanning electron microscopy (SBF-SEM) at nanometer resolution. Shown are 3 anatomical landmarks: the portal vein, the bile duct, and hepatocyte organelle structures (on a subcellular scale) with mitochondria, cell nuclei, plasma membranes, and the endoplasmic reticulum."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3D Visualizations Within the Human Reference Atlas",
